# Defect 069, repaired 2026-09-20 at M-declared-extents step 12.
#
# SYMPTOM. A C function's name standing as a callback argument was `check` exit
# 0, `build` exit 0, and `run` exit 134 with `panic: entered unreachable code —
# this is a compiler bug, please report it`, three runs of three.
#
# CAUSE. `emit/inst.hero`'s `.func_ref` arm wrote
# `hero_unreachable(); /* the gate refuses this form */` for an `extern_fn`
# callee, and the emitter then emitted the CALL four lines later anyway, passing
# a temporary nothing had assigned. A gate that refuses a form and then emits it
# is not a gate: it moves a compile-time question to run time and blames the
# compiler for the program.
#
# The repair is emission and not refusal, and the reason is that **clang is
# already the judge**: an extern's name is unmangled by design (CLAUDE.md §7),
# so assigning it to the parameter's own typedef is checked against the real
# header, and a mismatched signature is `incompatible function pointer types` at
# exit 1 — `.claude/rules/c-boundary.md`'s fifth clang-failure class arriving at
# an assignment instead of at a call.
#
# WHY THIS SHAPE AND NOT A SMALLER ONE. Panel 169 found that a destructor
# callback is the one mechanism every real C library offers for the retention
# problem defects 066 and 068 are about, and that Heroes could not pass one — so
# this case is the ladder's own shape, a buffer handed over with the function
# that disposes of it, rather than a callback that merely prints. The counter is
# what makes it an assertion: a callback never called leaves `blob_frees` at
# zero, and a callback whose address was a garbage temporary never reaches C.

extern "fixedbugs-a-c-function-crosses-as-a-callback.h"
    function blob_make() -> ptr
    function blob_take(p: ptr, n: i64, d: (function(ptr) -> ()))
    function counting_free(p: ptr)
    function blob_first() -> i64
    function blob_frees() -> i64

function main()
    b: ptr @ blob_make()

    # The line the defect was about: `counting_free` is a C function's NAME
    # standing as a value, and C is the one that calls it.
    blob_take(p: b, n: 4, d: counting_free)

    # C read the bytes before disposing of them.
    print(blob_first())

    # And C called the disposer Heroes named, exactly once.
    print(blob_frees())
